"sibionics.glucoseModelFooter" = "Stock is the manufacturer's algorithm. Balanced (from JugglucoNG) smooths the stock value's small 0.1 mmol/L steps and follows it at once on a real change, a turn or a low. Responsive (from JugglucoNG) tracks glucose and its speed and leans a little ahead of a trend, never far from the stock value. Adaptive V1 (from JugglucoNG) follows the sensor's chemical signal with two motion models and returns to the stock value whenever the evidence weakens; it shows the stock value for the first two hours. Adaptive V2 is an experimental estimator from JugglucoNG: it works from the sensor's calibrated signal before the manufacturer's display filtering, follows changes sooner and is less smooth. A minute it cannot estimate shows the stock value. Changing the model recalculates the sensor's history. Compare with a meter before relying on it.";
